  "text_md": "CM-FECL3 -E\n\nRevision 2\n\nsupersedes: Revision\n\nissued: 2019-04-17\n\nreviewed:\n\ndated: 2016-09-06\n\n## Product Specification\n\n## FERRIC CHLORIDE ANHYDROUS\n\nPRD-NO.: 30042332\n\n## 1 General\n\naccording to ISO 9001.\n\nAppearance:\n\ndark green to black crystalline powder\n\nChemical Name:\n\nferric chloride; FeCl3\n\nCAS-Nr:\n\n7705-08-0\n\nEINECS-Nr.:\n\n231-729-4\n\n## 2 Properties\n\n| Parameter   | Unit   | Specification   | Test method   |\n|-------------|--------|-----------------|---------------|\n| FeCl3       | 9/100g | min. 98.7       | Calculated    |\n| Fe (total)  | 9/100g | min. 34.0       | ICPIAES       |\n|             | 9/1009 | max 0.3         | Titration     |\n| Insolubles  | 9/1009 | max.0.2         | Gravimetry    |\n| As          | mglkg  | max.10          | AAS           |\n| Cr          | mglkg  | max.500         | ICPIAES       |\n| Cu          | mglkg  | max.120         | ICPIAES       |\n| Mn          | 9/1009 | max.0.2         | ICPIAES       |\n| Ni          | mglkg  | max.300         | ICPIAES       |\n| Pb          | mglkg  | max 10          | ICPIAES       |\n| Zn          | mglkg  | max. 400        | ICPIAES       |\n\nThe aforementioned data shall constitute the agreed contractual quality of the product at the time of passing of risk. The data are controlled at regular intervals as part of our quality assurance program Neither these data nor the properties of product specimens shall imply any legally binding guarantee of certain properties or of fitness for a specific purpose. No liability of ours can be derived therefrom.\n\n<!-- image -->",
